    {
      "id": 2270,
      "sender_id": 362,
      "content": "<p>Hi all,</p>\n<p>Inspired by Thomas Bloom's <a href=\"https://www.erdosproblems.com/\">Erdős Problems</a>, I built a preprint server designed to host AI-generated mathematical papers. My main motivation was to create a place for papers like the OpenAI writeup about the unit distance problem.</p>\n<p>Here's a <a href=\"https://open-author.vercel.app/about\">prototype</a>. There are only dummy papers so far, but the core features are live: one can create accounts, submit papers and review the work of others. Feel free to try it out.</p>\n<p>I’m curious to hear your thoughts. Could a platform like this become a useful piece of mathematical infrastructure? And if so, what design decisions matter most?</p>",
      "recipient_id": 24,
      "timestamp": 1781297591,
      "client": "website",
