    {
      "id": 3746,
      "sender_id": 396,
      "content": "<p>There is a massive delay in computing the discriminants. Computing the Galois group is much faster. Also note that no one's polynomials are scored at the moment. The scores are basically flat-lined. It is possible that they prioritise computing the Galois groups over the discriminants at the moment (and updating the scores). Using the submissions tab/API, you can see whether SAIR's Galois group computation matches your expectation. I would presume the deadline/end of competition is for uploading polynomials. It will then take some time to score the backlog.   <br>\n<img alt=\"image.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"604x478\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/5/58/8pbjpRZ0qYkHBkA7qSxu99gB/image.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/5/58/8pbjpRZ0qYkHBkA7qSxu99gB/image.png/840x560.webp\"></p>",
